# Environment Variables

GitHub API access and MCP server authentication are separate:

- GitHub API access uses `GITHUB_TOKEN_MODE` to choose either `GITHUB_PAT` or a per-request GitHub PAT header.
- MCP server authentication uses `MCP_AUTH_MODE` with `MCP_API_TOKEN`, GitHub OAuth, or both.

| Variable | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GITHUB_TOKEN_MODE` | No (default: `env`) | GitHub PAT source: `env`, `request`, or `request_or_env` |
| `GITHUB_PAT_HEADER` | No (default: `X-GitHub-PAT`) | Header for request-scoped GitHub PATs. Must not be `Authorization` |
| `GITHUB_CLIENT_CACHE_MAX_SIZE` | No (default: `128`) | Max cached request-scoped GitHub clients; least-recently-used clients are closed on eviction |
| `GITHUB_CLIENT_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS` | No (default: `1800`) | Idle TTL for cached request-scoped GitHub clients; expired clients are closed |
| `GITHUB_VALIDATE_REQUEST_PAT` | No (default: `true`) | Validate each new request PAT with GitHub `/user` before caching |
| `GITHUB_PAT` | When `GITHUB_TOKEN_MODE=env`; optional fallback for `request_or_env` | Server-level GitHub PAT. **Read-only tools**: classic `public_repo`/`repo`; fine-grained `Contents: Read` + `Metadata: Read`. **Write tools**: classic `repo`; fine-grained `Contents: Read+Write` + `Metadata: Read` + `Pull requests: Read+Write` + `Actions: Read+Write` |
| `MCP_READ_ONLY` | No (default: `false`) | `true` = disable all write/PR/CI tools at startup |
| `MCP_AUTH_MODE` | No (default: `both`) | `token`, `oauth`, or `both` |
| `MCP_API_TOKEN` | When mode is `token` or `both` | Static bearer token for clients |
| `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` | When mode is `oauth` or `both` | GitHub OAuth App client ID |
| `GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET` | When mode is `oauth` or `both` | GitHub OAuth App client secret |
| `BASE_URL` | When mode is `oauth` or `both` | Public URL of this server (for OAuth callbacks) |
| `GITHUB_OAUTH_SCOPES` | No (default: `user`) | Comma-separated OAuth scopes |
| `ALLOWED_GITHUB_LOGINS` | No | Comma-separated GitHub logins allowed via OAuth; empty = all users |
| `FASTMCP_HOME` | No | Writable directory for persistent OAuth storage; unset = in-memory |
| `MCP_AUTH_AUDIT_LOG` | No (default: `true`) | Log auth decisions (never logs token values) |
| `MCP_STATELESS` | No (default: `true`) | `true` = stateless; `false` = stateful SSE replay via Redis (requires Upstash vars) |
| `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` | When `MCP_STATELESS=false` | Upstash REST URL |
| `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN` | When `MCP_STATELESS=false` | Upstash REST token |
| `HOST` | No (default: `0.0.0.0`) | Bind address |
| `PORT` | No (default: `8000`) | Bind port |

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in values before running.

## Auth Modes

- **`token`** — static `MCP_API_TOKEN` only (DebugTokenVerifier with constant-time compare)
- **`oauth`** — GitHub OAuth 2.1 proxy (GitHubProvider) + raw OAuth 2.0 token fallback (GitHubTokenVerifier)
- **`both`** (default) — all three auth methods via MultiAuth: proxy, static token, raw token

## GitHub Token Modes

- **`env`** (default) — use `GITHUB_PAT` for every GitHub API call.
- **`request`** — require each MCP request to send `GITHUB_PAT_HEADER`.
- **`request_or_env`** — use the request header first, then fall back to `GITHUB_PAT`.

Use a separate header such as `X-GitHub-PAT` for GitHub access. `Authorization` is reserved for MCP server authentication.

In request modes, the server caches one GitHub client per distinct PAT with LRU and TTL eviction. Evicted clients are closed, and new request PATs are validated by default.
